\pard\sa120\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs20\cf2\b THE VEDANTA  \u183?  EMPLOYMENT  \u183?  YASHAR\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa120\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs36\cf1\b Yashar \u8212? what you have to do\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa120\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs22 Follow Head Chef Shyam\u8217?s kitchen programme. Learn it, then do it in this order every shift.\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa120\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs22\b You follow the daily. You do not skip date-check. You do not skip the recipe. 20 guests is not 20 jobs.\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa120\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs28\cf1\b 1. What you have to do\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa120\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs22 1. Open the kitchen safe (temps + date check) before you cook.\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa120\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs22 2. Confirm today\u8217?s guest number and today\u8217?s diets \u8212? they change (10, 20, 30, 50).\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa120\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs22 3. Follow today\u8217?s menu and recipes \u8212? do not guess.\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa120\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs22 4. For every dish: calculate, collect, prep, cook, label, wash.\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa120\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs22 5. Help breakfast, lunch and dinner be ready on time.\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa120\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs22 6. Clean as you go. Date-check again at close.\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa120\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs22 7. If you are the only person on the board, say so early. Do not silently work 07:00 to 21:00.\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa120\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs22 8. Kitchen = food on the pass. Tea, buffet dressing and dining-room wash are not your default job.\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa120\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs28\cf1\b 2. What you have to learn\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa120\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs22 One dish is about 10 jobs. If you only cook, you are late.\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa120\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs22 Starter to dessert is often 6 items \u8212? six recipes, not one pot.\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa120\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs22 Guests are not fixed: 10, 20, 30 or 50. Prep today\u8217?s number, not last week\u8217?s 50.\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa120\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs22 Extra diets = extra work. Write them down.\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa120\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs22 Recipe first: calculate each ingredient, then collect, then prep.\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa120\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs22 HACCP every day: temps and date-check, 10 guests or 50.\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa120\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs22 If the board is empty, you cook and wash. Ask for a wash window or a simpler menu.\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa120\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs28\cf1\b 3. How to follow the daily (in this order)\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa120\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs22 Arrive: clock in, uniform, hands, read the day board.\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa120\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs22 Step 1 \u8212? Open safe: temps, date-check, pull out-of-date food, report broken kit.\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa120\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs22 Step 2 \u8212? Lock today\u8217?s number and diets in writing before big prep.\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa120\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs22 Step 3 \u8212? Cook this menu for this guest count with this staff. Alone = simpler menu.\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa120\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs22 Step 4 \u8212? Calculate: portion x today\u8217?s guests, then add each extra diet line.\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa120\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs22 Step 5 \u8212? Collect the pick-list first, then wash, cut and weigh.\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa120\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs22 Step 6 \u8212? Breakfast, lunch, dinner. Handover on time. Wash Kitchen pots.\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa120\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs22 Step 7 \u8212? Write shortages, clean, label, date-check again.\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa120\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs22 Step 8 \u8212? Close. A chef who finishes at 21:00 is not on at 07:00 the next day.\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa120\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs28\cf1\b 4. Your clock\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa120\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs22 Morning 07:00-16:00 \u8212? open, breakfast, lunch, handover.\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa120\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs22 Late 12:00-21:00 \u8212? handover, dinner, Kitchen close.\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa120\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs22 Early KA/KP 07:00-15:00 \u8212? prep support, deliveries, Kitchen wash.\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa120\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs22 Late KA/KP 15:00-22:00 \u8212? dinner support and Kitchen close.\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa120\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs22 10 guests = same steps, fewer portions. 30 or 50 = you cannot be chef and porter.\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa120\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs28\cf1\b 5. This week\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa120\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs22 Day 1-2: shadow the open. Count the ten elements on one dish.\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa120\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs22 Day 3-5: calculate one recipe. Collect a full pick-list. Run Kitchen wash in service.\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa120\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs22 Week 2: lead one prep block. Write a handover. Diet swap only from the written list.\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa120\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs28\cf1\b 6. If you get stuck\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa120\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs22 No guest number: stop big prep. Ask Shyam or the Duty Manager.\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa120\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs22 Diet added in service: tell Shyam. Simple substitute if he says so.\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa120\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs22 You are alone on a full menu: say it. Safe small menu beats a late unsafe menu.\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa120\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs22 Asked to do Restaurant wash while Kitchen pots are out: Kitchen pots first.\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa120\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs22 Asked to start at 07:00 after a 21:00 finish: no. Tell Shyam or the Duty Manager.\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa120\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs22 Kitchen owns the food. Restaurant owns guest-facing dining and refreshment. Yashar follows the daily in order.\b0\cf0\par
